interviewQuestions.a:
Nothing at the data layer changes — same tools, resources, prompts, same JSON-RPC shapes. Everything that changes is transport-layer:
- swap `stdio` for `streamable-http`;
- add real auth (OAuth), since a process boundary is no longer your trust boundary;
- handle concurrent sessions via `Mcp-Session-Id`, and decide stateless servers vs. sticky routing behind a load balancer;
- add standard HTTP hardening (TLS, origin/CORS checks) and observability for failure modes stdio never had — under stdio the only "failure" was the child process dying; under HTTP you inherit timeouts, retries, and partial failures.
